   "evidence": "Mathlib names a power of an expression with a trailing `_pow` (`neg_one_pow`, `Units.conj_pow`, which this PR uses). A leading `pow_` means the exponent is the compound expression (`pow_succ : a ^ (n + 1) = \u2026`, `pow_mul : a ^ (m * n) = \u2026`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/Nilpotent/UnipotentRoot.lean",
   "fix": "Rename to `Units.nilpotentExpUnit_inv_smul_log_zpow` and update its use in `existsUnique_isNilpotent_sub_one_and_zpow_eq`.",
   "issue": "`Units.zpow_nilpotentExpUnit_inv_smul_log` proves `nilpotentExpUnit (...) ^ m = u`. A leading `zpow_` reads as `a ^ (nilpotentExpUnit \u2026)`, so the name puts the root in the exponent.",
   "line": 50
  }
 ],
